        },
        "message": "Sensors override v4: lock-free busy check \u2014 the render thread holds renderMutex around the ENTIRE sensorManager.RunOnce\n\nsensors-override-stallprobe-1 (thread probe with per-thread\nwchan/syscall) pinned the final blocking site: through the ~109 ms\nstall the physics thread futex-waits on the HEAP renderMutex\n(0x55cdcf5f82b4) while the render thread burns a full core \u2014 because\nRunOnce holds renderMutex around the ENTIRE sensorManager.RunOnce()\n(render + publish), and the v3 busy check still acquired that mutex\nbefore reading the flag. Same acquisition-class bug as v2, second\nmutex.\n\nv4: the busy flags (running, updateAvailable) are std::atomic \u2014 the\ncheck reads them WITHOUT the mutex. The arm block still takes\nrenderMutex, but only when no render is in flight (the render thread\nthen sits in its 1 ms poll with the mutex released), so that\nacquisition is bounded. All three physics/render coupling points are\nnow genuinely non-blocking: ECM sync (try_to_lock renderUtilMutex),\nbusy check (lock-free atomics), arming (reached only when idle)."
      },
      "type": "Git"
    },
